INSERT INTO public.chunks (id, content, source, page, embedding) VALUES (181, 'It doesn''t return a large `str` containing the data in JSON format (as a string). It returns a Python standard data structure (e.g. a `dict`) with values and sub-values that are all compatible with JSON.

/// note

`jsonable_encoder` is actually used by **FastAPI** internally to convert data. But it is useful in many other scenarios.

