INSERT INTO public.chunks (id, content, source, page, embedding) VALUES (428, 'You can declare that a parameter can accept `None`, but that it''s still required. This would force clients to send a value, even if the value is `None`.

To do that, you can declare that `None` is a valid type but simply do not declare a default value:

{* ../../docs_src/query_params_str_validations/tutorial006c_an_py310.py hl[9] *}

